ge !== 'requested-input': Render as collapsible section, collapsed by default\n\n3. **Use existing CSS pattern** from stage toggles:\n   - Apply `.stage-toggle.collapsed` and `.stage-body.hidden` classes\n   - Ensure toggle icons rotate appropriately\n\n4. **Accessibility**:\n   - Add `aria-expanded` attributes to toggle buttons\n   - Add `aria-controls` linking toggles to content sections\n   - Ensure keyboard navigation (Enter/Space to toggle)\n   - Add `role=\"region\"` to collapsible content areas\n\n5. **Handle long content**:\n   - Add `max-height` and `overflow-y: auto` to collapsible content containers\n   - Smooth transition on expand/collapse\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: TUI Implementation\n\n1. **Verify Textual Collapsible widget**:\n   - Check that Textual version supports `Collapsible` widget (available since v0.37.0)\n   - If not available, implement custom collapsible using `CollapsibleGroup` or toggle behavior\n\n2. **Modify `_feature_markdown()` in `tui.py:100-150`**:\n   - Replace flat Markdown rendering with structured layout using Widgets\n   - Use Textual's `Collapsible` widget for each section\n\n3. **TUI Section Structure**:\n   - Always visible: Title, Description (rendered outside collapsibles)\n   - Collapsible sections:\n     - History (default: expanded)\n     - Plan (default: collapsed)\n     - Implementation Spec (impl_spec) (default: collapsed)\n     - Test Spec (test_spec) (default: collapsed)\n     - Implementation Notes (impl_notes) (default: collapsed)\n     - Questions for Human (default: collapsed)\n   - Exclude Pipeline Log (confirmed: only actual Item Details)\n\n4. **Empty section handling**:\n   - Show section header with collapse icon\n   - Display \"No [section] provided\" text inside collapsed section\n\n5. **Styling**:\n   - Match existing TUI theme (colors, borders)\n   - Ensure toggle indicators are visible\n   - Add keyboard shortcuts for expand/collapse (optional: arrow keys)\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Testing\n\n1. **Test empt